// Test: bugfixes/codegen_stack_remaining_static_call_to_void_method
// Grammar: static_method_call → ClassName.method(args)  (grammar.ebnf §5
//   static_method_call) where the resolved static method has a void return
//   type.
// Regression: CODEGEN_STACK_REMAINING (dashboard fp 82badd8d3d63).
//   Follow-up to 618571c5 (fp df5b8c9b1021). After that fix propagated
//   user-class static method return types through the typechecker, calls
//   to void methods like `ClassName.log(msg)` reached the MIR builder's
//   StaticMethodCall arm with `expression.expr_type = ConcreteType::Null`
//   (the canonical void marker). That arm unconditionally emitted the
//   Call instruction with `dest = Some(result_id)`, so the codegen then
//   wrote `local.set` after a no-result WASM `call` → wasmparser failed
//   the module with "type mismatch: expected i32 but nothing on stack".
//   The instance-MethodCall arm already had the matching void check.
//
//   Fix: mirror the MethodCall arm's void detection
//   (Null / Undefined / MirType::Void / MirType::Ptr(Void)) in the
//   StaticMethodCall arm and set `dest = None` for void calls so codegen
//   omits the local.set entirely.
//
// Expected output:
//   hello from void static
//   after void static
//   hi from chained
//   after chained

start:
	C1.log("hello from void static")
	print("after void static")
	C1.both("hi from chained")
	print("after chained")

class C1
	functions:
		log(string msg)
			print(msg)
		both(string msg)
			log(msg)
